Subject: Raise an R condition instead of terminating the R session on panic

libmdbx's osal_panic() calls the platform assert-failure entry point and then
abort() on POSIX, or _CrtDbgReport/DebugBreak/FatalExit on Windows. Every one of
those takes the whole R session down with it, and `R CMD check` flags the
resulting __assert_fail / __assert_rtn references under "checking compiled code".

Route the panic through mdbx_r_panic(), implemented in src/r_mdbx_hooks.cpp.
Package calls run below a package-owned jump boundary: the hook records the
failure and returns to that boundary, an optional callback poisons the owning
handle, and only then does the cpp11 layer raise an R condition. The enclosing
while(1) is retained so the compiler still treats osal_panic() as non-returning.

Caveat: the jump out of libmdbx may leave internal locks held. A panic means an
invariant was already violated, so the poison callback must make the environment
unusable and its finalizer must not re-enter libmdbx.

Note this leaves the per-platform __assert_fail declaration block above as dead
code. It is deliberately left in place to keep the patch minimal; declarations
alone create no symbol references, only calls do.

--- a/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
+++ b/src/vendor/libmdbx/mdbx.c
@@ -29613,26 +29613,16 @@
 #define __assert_fail(assertion, file, line, function) __assert(function, file, line, assertion)
 
 #endif /* __assert_fail */
+
+/* R package patch: implemented in src/r_mdbx_hooks.cpp. See tools/patches. */
+extern void mdbx_r_panic(const char *msg, const char *func, unsigned line);
 
 __cold void osal_panic(const char *msg, const char *func, unsigned line) {
   while (1) {
-#if IS_WINDOWS
-#if defined(_DEBUG) && !MDBX_WITHOUT_MSVC_CRT
-    _CrtDbgReport(_CRT_ASSERT, func, line, "libmdbx", "assertion failed: %s", msg);
-#else
-    char *message = nullptr;
-    const int num = osal_asprintf(&message, "\r\nMDBX-ASSERTION: %s, %s:%u\r\n", msg, func, line);
-    if (num < 1 || !message)
-      message = "\r\n<asprintf() failed>\r\n";
-    OutputDebugStringA(message);
-#endif
-    if (IsDebuggerPresent())
-      DebugBreak();
-    FatalExit(STATUS_ASSERTION_FAILURE);
-#else
-    __assert_fail(msg, "libmdbx", line, func);
-    abort();
-#endif
+    /* R package patch: return to a package-owned guard rather than calling the
+     * platform assert handler / abort() / FatalExit(), all of which would take
+     * whole R session down. mdbx_r_panic() does not return. */
+    mdbx_r_panic(msg, func, line);
   }
 }
 
